# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
/target/
/gen/schemas

# Generated by `tauri android init` — the CI Android job (build-android in
# .github/workflows/tauri-build.yml) regenerates this fresh every run rather
# than committing it. Ignored here too so a local `tauri android init` (e.g.
# from the offline project zip) doesn't accidentally get checked in.
/gen/android

# `cargo vendor` output + its offline-source override, generated on-demand
# for the "everything included" offline project zip (see chat/delivery, not
# part of normal dev). NEVER commit these to the repo — a checked-in
# .cargo/config.toml pointing at a vendor/ directory that doesn't exist in
# git would break every build, including CI. Regenerate locally with:
#   cd src-tauri && cargo vendor vendor
/vendor
/.cargo
